FAIL  Disk space          only 3 GB free on the drive that holds Puddle's data (/home/dev/.local/share/puddle), under the 5 GB line
      fix:  Workspace volumes and root disks, package caches and builds inside a workspace all
            grow on this drive, and a full drive stops them with errors that do not name the
            cause (a build that dies halfway, a tool that cannot write). This check measures the
            room left on the drive, not the sizes of the workspaces' disks: a root disk or a
            volume is a sparse file, so its size is a limit and takes space only as the
            workspace writes, and the workspaces can still grow past what is left. Free space
            before you start or build anything in a workspace: delete workspaces you no longer
            use and files you do not need. The line is the setting "Fail when free space is
            under" in Settings.
ok    Disk encryption     data drive encrypted (BitLocker); swap /dev/dm-1 encrypted (BitLocker)
ok    SSH agent           the agent on /run/user/1000/agent.sock holds 1 key (ed25519: 1)
ok    Azure CLI (az)      version 2.64.0
ok    Credential store    the operating system's credential store: a test write and delete worked

1 problem to fix before Puddle can run sandboxes. (1.2 s)

