      "fix": "Workspace volumes and root disks, package caches and builds inside a workspace all grow on this drive, and a full drive stops them with errors that do not name the cause (a build that dies halfway, a tool that cannot write). This check measures the room left on the drive, not the sizes of the workspaces' disks: a root disk or a volume is a sparse file, so its size is a limit and takes space only as the workspace writes, and the workspaces can still grow past what is left. Free space before you start or build anything in a workspace: delete workspaces you no longer use and files you do not need. The line is the setting \"Fail when free space is under\" in Settings."
